## Remove the server

```
claude mcp remove {{ serverData.id }} --scope project
```

Then delete the `.mcp-servers/{{ serverData.name }}` file.

## Install the server for all the projects of one user

Do this only if the user asks for it. It changes the configuration of the user, and not the
configuration of the project.

```
claude mcp add {{ serverData.id }} --scope user -- dotnet run <ABSOLUTE_PATH>/{{ serverData.name }} -v q
```

At this scope, the path must be absolute, because each project has a different working directory.
Keep the file in a permanent directory. Do not move the file, because the configuration contains the
path.

## Notes

- Keep the `-v q` option. Standard output carries the JSON-RPC stream. Without `-v q`, the build
  output can come to that stream and break the protocol. It is two elements, `"-v"` and `"q"`. It is
  not one element `"-v q"`.
{%- if serverData.id == "image-utility" %}
- This server keeps each file path in its working directory, and refuses a path outside that
  directory. With a project installation, that directory is the project.
{%- endif %}
